---
import Layout from '../../layouts/Layout.astro';
import Callout from '../../components/Callout.astro';
import EventStream from '../../components/EventStream.astro';
import PageNext from '../../components/PageNext.astro';
import CtaBlock from '../../components/CtaBlock.astro';
---

<Layout title="Failure learning — a fix learned once propagates" pathname="/features/learn">
  <section class="page-head">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="eyebrow-chain">
        <span class="eyebrow">Feature</span>
        <span class="eyebrow-sep">·</span>
        <span class="eyebrow-dim">maddu learn</span>
        <span class="eyebrow-sep">·</span>
        <span class="eyebrow-dim">since v1.90.0</span>
      </div>
      <h1>Solve it once. <span class="dim-h1">Carry it everywhere.</span></h1>
      <p class="lede">
        A mistake corrected in one session becomes a durable rule the next agent already knows — and, when it recurs across repos, a correction your whole fleet inherits.
      </p>
      <pre class="feat-cli"><code>$ maddu learn
distilled 4 corrections · 2 project facts → CLAUDE.md · 2 patterns → memory</code></pre>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="container">
      <header class="section-head">
        <span class="eyebrow">§ 01 · The problem</span>
        <h2>The same mistake, in every fresh session.</h2>
        <p>
          A hard-won fix lives in one transcript, then evaporates. The next agent — a fresh context, or a different repo entirely — rediscovers the same wrong turn, because nothing turned that experience into a rule it could read first.
        </p>
      </header>

      <div class="grid-3">
        <div class="panel">
          <div class="panel-head">
            <span class="panel-title">Mined from what failed</span>
            <span class="panel-aside">typed</span>
          </div>
          <p><code>learn</code> reads past sessions for failed→succeeded tool-call pairs and distils typed corrections: stable project facts go to the project's <code>CLAUDE.md</code>; volatile patterns go to queryable memory.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="panel">
          <div class="panel-head">
            <span class="panel-title">Federated across repos</span>
            <span class="panel-aside">approval-only</span>
          </div>
          <p><code>learn sync</code> shares the portable corrections — a lesson recurring in ≥2 repos, or tagged <code>@portable</code>. Adopted on approval only, redacted before it travels.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="panel">
          <div class="panel-head">
            <span class="panel-title">Vendor memory, imported</span>
            <span class="panel-aside">since v1.90.0</span>
          </div>
          <p><code>learn sync --from-claude-memory</code> imports Claude Code's auto-memory as provenance-carrying facts. Import-only by contract — the vendor directory is never written — and content-hash-deduped, so re-running is idempotent.</p>
        </div>
      </div>

      <Callout tone="ok" title="A claim of done needs proof" tag="completion-claim-gate">
        <p>
          A deterministic completion-claim gate flags hedged "done" claims — "should work", "seems to pass" — that carry no observed proof. It's evidence, not a model checking a model: the record either shows the run or it doesn't.
        </p>
      </Callout>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="container">
      <header class="section-head">
        <span class="eyebrow">§ 02 · On the record</span>
        <h2>What learning and federating looks like on the spine.</h2>
      </header>
      <EventStream
        eyebrow="Distil, import, then federate"
        source=".maddu/events/2026-07-05.ndjson"
        entries={[
          { time: '15:41:12.006', type: 'LESSON_DISTILLED',         tone: 'accent',   payload: 'pair=eslint-flat-config · target=CLAUDE.md · type=project-fact', actor: 'claude-code' },
          { time: '15:41:12.220', type: 'VENDOR_MEMORY_IMPORTED',   tone: 'session',  payload: 'source=claude-memory · adopted=3 · deduped=5 · preview=false', actor: 'claude-code' },
          { time: '15:52:03.771', type: 'LESSON_FEDERATED',         tone: 'ok',        payload: 'lesson=win-path-quoting · repos=3 · redacted · approved', actor: 'operator' },
        ]}
      />
      <p class="feat-note">
        Preview is the default; <code>--adopt</code> writes. Each import rides a <code>VENDOR_MEMORY_IMPORTED</code> event, so a memory rebuild replays the corpus faithfully from the record.
      </p>
      <p class="feat-note">
        Related verbs: <a href="/capabilities/learn"><code>maddu learn</code></a> · <a href="/capabilities/memory"><code>maddu memory</code></a> · <a href="/capabilities/skill"><code>maddu skill</code></a> · <a href="/capabilities/blueprint"><code>maddu blueprint</code></a>
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <PageNext
    eyebrow="Next feature"
    title="Fleet view — know which of your installs are stale, offline."
    hint="One glance across every registered workspace: version, freshness, last activity."
    href="/features/fleet"
    tone="accent"
  />
  <CtaBlock />
</Layout>

<style>
  .feat-cli {
    margin: var(--m-space-5) 0 0;
    padding: var(--m-space-4) var(--m-space-5);
    background: var(--m-bg-2);
    border: 1px solid var(--m-line);
    border-left: 2px solid var(--m-accent);
    border-radius: var(--m-radius);
    font-family: var(--m-font-mono);
    font-size: 13px;
    line-height: 1.7;
    color: var(--m-fg-1);
    overflow-x: auto;
  }
  .feat-note {
    margin-top: var(--m-space-5);
    font-size: 13px;
    color: var(--m-fg-2);
  }
  .feat-note code { font-size: 12px; }
</style>
